{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080784-alternate-legacy-attainments","id":1080784,"title":"Alternate Legacy Attainments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-19T01:43:26-07:00","id":1080784,"title":"Alternate Legacy Attainments","content":"So the book mentions that you can craft alternate Legacy Attainments instead of making watered down version of spells. It also says that these should be on par with a normal attainments.<br /> <br /> And... that's about it. No guidelines or examples of any kind. I am intrigued by this idea since I honestly find RAW Legacy Attainments just a bit too lacklustre, especially on their own, but I am not at all certain how to design these alternate attainments so they are on par with normal ones. I was hoping for some advice or examples.<br /> <br /> Below are some alternate attainments I can think of, are they mechanically valid?<br /> <br /> <b>An attainment that can act as a Yantra or improve a Yantra for a specific spell</b> (a storm-themed Legacy becomes one with natural storms, which increases the value of appropriate Environment Yantras by +1 or +2)<br /> <b>An attainment that allows you to spend Mana to improve one specific spell factor in a specific Arcanum</b> (a Time-focused Legacy learns esoteric secrets of Time, allowing them to lengthen the duration of all Time spells at the cost of 1 Mana)<br /> <b>An attainment that improves or adds to another attainment</b> (a Prime-focused Legacy that also possesses the Trained Observer Merit can use it's effects of 9-again or 8-again on a specific Prime spell to notice the truth, such as Pierce Deception)<br /> <b>An attainment that allows you to improve an Attribute or Skill above the maximum allowed value</b> (a transhumanist-themed Legacy learns the secrets of how to make magic TRULY break human limitations)<br /> <b>An attainment that allows you to rewrite rules </b>(a mathematics and probability-based Legacy that allows you to use Science instead of Athletics as Defense against attacks, maybe even versus firearms)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 04-19-2017, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T03:35:32-07:00","id":1080806,"title":"","content":"Here are my thoughts about the examples given:<br /> <br /> Yantra attainment: Legacies already have unique Yantras that you get on initiation, so I would say that being in an electrical storm simply acts as a +2 environment Yantra.<br /> <br /> Spend Mana for spell factors: Time 4 already does the effect you're describing. You can spend 1 Mana to apply Advanced Duration instead of using a Reach.<br /> <br /> Attainment that improves other attainments: This could fit into the Alternate Attainment rules, I think. Maybe generalize it to apply the effects of a Prime 3 spell to certain skill checks?<br /> <br /> Improving attribute or skill above maximum: Spells that increase/grant attributes or skills can increase them over the natural limit by spending 1 Mana. So, this actually fits into the regular Legacy Attainment rules.<br /> <br /> Rewriting rules attainment: I think the example you give would definitely fall under the category of &quot;Alternate Legacy Attainments.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternate Attainments are best used for unusual legacies, reapers, and Scelesti. An example of an usual legacy might be a group of mages who seek to free themselves from bodily confines and go into the Astral. Eventually they gain weird attainments that allow them to separate from their bodies in a more permanent way. Legacies that can travel to other realms easily also have Alternate Attainments to get to these places (Walkers in the Mists for an example?). Most of the Attainments a Reaper or Scelesti get from their Legacies would be Alternate. There's some good examples of Reaper Legacies in 1st edition, including people who store souls on computer hardware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T05:41:48-07:00","id":1080847,"title":"","content":"I have been enlightened by others on this forum to understand that legacy attainments are generally superior to spells rather than inferior to them (&quot;watered down&quot;). They are less flexible with respect to Reach allocation. If you explain why you believe they're lackluster, you might find that you have an incorrect assumption regarding the rules.<br /> <br /> Generally when you want a legacy attainment that does not correspond to a published spell, you design the effect you want using creative thaumaturgy. You can fit most any effect into that scheme.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, as the rules state, it's between you and your ST. Your permitted to go beyond the scope of the rules, but different STs will rule differently about what makes sense for a particular chronicle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T11:12:06-07:00","id":1080996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080784-alternate-legacy-attainments?p=1080847#post1080847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been enlightened by others on this forum to understand that legacy attainments are generally superior to spells rather than inferior to them (&amp;quot;watered down&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. They are less flexible with respect to Reach allocation. If you explain why you believe they're lackluster, you might find that you have an incorrect assumption regarding the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to be proven wrong in my assumption. I enjoyed reading your breakdown of Attainments in your recent thread, as well. I think what makes me regard them as watered down compared to just buying Praxes is my perception that less flexible = inferior in a game of creative spellcasting. To me they seem to mostly serve the purpose of giving you a couple of continual buffs, which is nice, while mechanically being like a &quot;get two, pay for one&quot; deal when purchasing Praxes, all the while hyping the concept that you reshape your entire being for one purpose.<br /> <br /> I know I express myself in a very vague and inane way, I'm sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T11:45:02-07:00","id":1081012,"title":"","content":"Well, they also give you some cool Paradox-free magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T11:54:14-07:00","id":1081016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080784-alternate-legacy-attainments?p=1080996#post1080996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to be proven wrong in my assumption. I enjoyed reading your breakdown of Attainments in your recent thread, as well. I think what makes me regard them as watered down compared to just buying Praxes is my perception that less flexible = inferior in a game of creative spellcasting. To me they seem to mostly serve the purpose of giving you a couple of continual buffs, which is nice, while mechanically being like a &quot;get two, pay for one&quot; deal when purchasing Praxes, all the while hyping the concept that you reshape your entire being for one purpose.<br /> <br /> I know I express myself in a very vague and inane way, I'm sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops you from continuing to use your flexible spell casting. Legacies cement your magical identity in a way that's -very- hard for reality to disrupt which is pretty much a requirement for any attempt to escape the Lie. The attainments should be looked at as nifty perks of carving out a place for your personal mythology in the Supernal, not the one stop shop for all the best magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:04:47-07:00","id":1081229,"title":"","content":"The main error in my understanding was from underestimating the number of primary spell factor ranks you have to work with due to misunderstanding the &quot;additional spell factors&quot; rule. If you seek to maximize ranks in primary spell factor, you can can have floor(1.5x - 1) where x is the dots in the relevant arcanum. So for a mage with e.g. Mind 4, that's 5 ranks in primary spell factor. If you design your attainments wisely that's pretty badass.<br /> <br /> Just because an effect isn't extremely flexible doesn't mean that it's not very useful -- specialized tools are powerful. Vampire Disciplines are less flexible than legacy attainments and they're still very useful too. You just need need to design the attainments that take advantage of the system. Legacy attainments are another tool in the toolbox alongside creative thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Being able to hurt or kill indiscriminately without risking Wisdom loss is awesome. You can do this with a well-designed Rank 3 legacy attainment. Hexes and other debuffs that cannot be dispelled are also awesome. Look at this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Rank 3 Attainment: Basically Fucked<br /> Fate, Ruling, Potency Primary, Withstood by Composure<br /> Reach allocated to Instant Casting and Advanced Duration<br /> <br /> Hex the subject with effects of the caster's choosing, one per Potency.</div>A caster with Fate 4 can reliably apply 2-3 tilts per turn to most subjects, they each last an hour, they can't be counterspelled or dispelled, there's no Wisdom loss for hurting another person, and there's no risk of paradox. You can make someone Blinded and Deafened. They generally will not be able to cast on you unless you're grappling with them as they won't be able to sense you, and they'll suffer significant dice penalties in combat. It's not world-ending, but it's undeniably useful and also flexible to a degree. This could be available to a character with Gnosis 4.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also if you redid the above as a Rank 5 attainment that granted boons, you can get +6 dice 6 spells each time you use it within an hour (the additional two reach allowed by making it Rank 5 go to enabling it to effect spellcasting rolls). That is in addition to bonuses from yantras and it can't be dispelled. That's also very strong and flexible, but who really ever gets Rank 5 attainments. vOv","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-20-2017, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:40:41-07:00","id":1081247,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with trying to make Attainments that aren't spells.... is that Awakened magic pretty much is billed as being able to do anything at all with the right Arcana levels and time to cast (ie big enough dice pool). Anything you make into an Attainment could just as easily be a spell. Calculating Defense based on a skill like Science is totally doable as a spell, and you're just going to end up with the same thing. Spells already allow you to break the normal human limits of attributes, or add 8-again to dice rolls on magic. Spending mana to improve spell factors is the only thing that's not a spell, and that's because its already established as reserved for Attainments - level 4 attainments, in fact. Its also reserved for paradox and scelesti manipulation. <br /> <br /> So, yeah. Manipulating Reaches is pretty much the only thing I can think of that's not basically a spell by another name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T19:52:45-07:00","id":1081254,"title":"","content":"If I remember right, a couple of Legacies like the Concord of Serpents and I think the Clavicularius could regain Willpower through their Attainments in ways spells couldn't manage. I assume the &quot;Strange Attainments&quot; sidebar refers to effects like those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T21:16:40-07:00","id":1081282,"title":"","content":"Also I suppose weird meta-gaming effects that break fundamental game systems, e.g. legacy attainments that:<ul><li>Modify Wisdom scores</li> <li>Modify Gnosis</li> <li>Pervert the Action economy</li> <li>Modify Arcana scores</li> <li>Change the ranks of Practices</li> <li>Directly grant experience</li> </ul>Some game systems obviously aren't meant to be subject to magical effects, and you also shouldn't be able to design legacy attainments that do these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T04:17:20-07:00","id":1081378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080784-alternate-legacy-attainments?p=1081254#post1081254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember right, a couple of Legacies like the Concord of Serpents and I think the Clavicularius could regain Willpower through their Attainments in ways spells couldn't manage. I assume the &quot;Strange Attainments&quot; sidebar refers to effects like those.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, they allowed you to regain willpower in a way that no publish spell did. Slight difference. There's absolutely nothing stopping you from making those effects as a spell if you absolutely wanted to.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, there aren't any Attainments from 1e that aren't basically just spells, or reproducable via Creative Thaumaturgy. Even in 2e, most of the example Attainments could just as easily been spells. Or are completely unnecessary as Attainments - yes, I'm looking at you Time 2. You should be ashamed of yourself. Shame upon you!<br /> <br /> If we can make the ability to hang spells as a Time spell instead of an attainment / conjunctional Arcana like in 1e? Then we can have pretty much all of the Attainments as spells. I think that they ended up with universal attainments because the game had a lot of &quot;add this conjunctional to do this effect&quot; and wanted to formalize them in one area. Which has led to some... strangeness involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T20:15:07-07:00","id":1081675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1080784-alternate-legacy-attainments?p=1081254#post1081254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember right, a couple of Legacies like the Concord of Serpents and I think the Clavicularius could regain Willpower through their Attainments in ways spells couldn't manage. I assume the &quot;Strange Attainments&quot; sidebar refers to effects like those.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion the quintessencial &quot;strange attainments&quot; were the crap that Legion had for Summoners. But even then some of them might be spells, but some of them were not so much spells as they were systems, kind of like how summoning itself is a weird system.<br /> <br /> I guess what would make a truly strange attainment would be getting something that's normally a system for another splat, like making pledges or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}